WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.700
Simon Kinberg isn't afraid to admit his mistakes.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:08.130
The director of Dark Phoenix did just that
when speaking to KCRW during an appearance

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.020
on the outlet's The Business podcast.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.100
Getting remarkably candid, the filmmaker took
the blame for everything that went wrong with

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:14.980
Dark Phoenix.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.200
"I'm here, I'm saying when a movie doesn't
work, put it on me.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.980
When a movie doesn't connect with audiences,
put it on me."

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.859
In the interview, Kinberg noted that it's
difficult to talk about Dark Phoenix in a

00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:27.730
negative context because he genuinely loves
the film.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.940
Ultimately, though, he feels the onus is on
him to take the blame for Dark Phoenix crashing

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.040
and burning with moviegoers and critics.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:37.880
As for what might have saved Dark Phoenix
from its grim fate, Kinberg doesn't believe

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.780
that there's anything that could have been
done to yield a different outcome.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.540
Would changing the film's release date yet
again have helped it?

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.600
Probably not, but Kinberg admitted that the
changing dates didn't help the film land on

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.480
the right foot:

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.360
"I always felt that we had a tough date for
this particular movie.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:55.510
It wasn't made as a classic superhero movie,
it was made as more of a dramatic, intimate,

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:56.340
smaller film.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.540
Originally it was going to come out in November
[2018], then it was going to come out in February

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:04.560
[2019], and those were the dates that I felt
like it actually would have felt more appropriate

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.400
to."

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.880
Did the massive box office success of Avengers:
Endgame, now the most profitable film of all

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.700
time, somehow impact Dark Phoenix's performance
when it opened June 7th?

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:18.320
Maybe, but Kinberg just can't get behind the
idea that another film is to blame for Dark

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.140
Phoenix's bombing.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.020
The director said:

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.180
"Coming out five, six weeks after what may
well be the biggest movie or the second biggest

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:28.770
movie in the history of cinema, that also
happens to be also in the genre of superheroes,

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.950
was tough for us, and I always anticipated
that it was going to be tough to be in the

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.290
tailwinds of that movie.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.820
But I wouldn't blame it on the weekend."

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.579
The tense atmosphere behind the scenes at
Fox following their merger with Disney didn't

00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:40.930
make production on Dark Phoenix easy either.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:45.180
Apparently, the layoffs taking place at that
time affected several of the studio's important

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:45.880
arms.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.900
Kinberg continued,

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:51.299
"The marketing and publicity side of Fox were
very badly hit, and I noticed it because […] I

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.280
was going to marketing meetings every week
and there were people who weren't there anymore."

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.299
Kinberg also shared that he's actively trying
to keep himself from thinking about how differently

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:03.440
Dark Phoenix may have fared if it wasn't delayed
or if it had been better marketed.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.300
At the end of the day, it doesn't matter:
what happened happened, and Kinberg is taking

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.640
it as a learning experience.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.940
"I mean honestly, there's no way to know,
and that's the thing that I think can drive

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.620
people crazy and keep them up and be thinking
about a movie's failure years later.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.140
If the lesson you've learned is that you had
the wrong date or you didn't have good marketing

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.400
— that's not a lesson."

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.420
Kinberg's comments here are refreshing.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.300
It's not often that the architect of a box
office bomb comes forward and admits that

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.780
he should shoulder part of the blame for a
film's failure.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.220
What's even more important here is Kinberg's
mention that Dark Phoenix floundering taught

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.040
him a lesson.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.040
The film will probably do the same for the
filmmakers Marvel Studios, who will be looking

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.240
to bring the X-Men and several other comic
book characters to the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.400
In working out the best way to introduce the
mutants in a whole new movie franchise, Marvel

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.900
can turn to Dark Phoenix and pinpoint the
exact things not to do.

